The test finds a frame by its index among [data-frame-surface] elements.
Our first load draws frames as shells until the page's camera rests
(0048), and a FrameShell has a surface too: for a moment after the load
each frame had a shell and a view, so index 1 was the left frame's view
and the pointer measured the selection to itself. Wait for the views, as
pageCanvas does since 0055.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 tests/measureBrowser.test.ts | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/tests/measureBrowser.test.ts b/tests/measureBrowser.test.ts
index 618dfca..51c6f80 100644
--- a/tests/measureBrowser.test.ts
+++ b/tests/measureBrowser.test.ts
@@ -23,6 +23,9 @@ describe.skipIf(!findBrowserPath())('⌥ distances', () => {
     page.setDefaultTimeout(10_000)
     await page.setViewport({ width: 1600, height: 1000 })
     await openCanvasPage(page, [LEFT, RIGHT])
+    /* the first load draws frames as shells until the camera rests, and a shell
+       has a [data-frame-surface] too: wait for the views before counting them */
+    await page.waitForFunction(() => !document.querySelector('[data-frame-shell]'))
   })
 
   /** a design point of a frame, on screen */
